/-!
# The affine-chart inputs of Stacks 06BH

Let `g : X' ⟶ Y'` be a morphism of algebraic spaces over a scheme `S` contained in a big fppf site
`B`, let `Y ⊆ Y'` be a first-order thickening with defining ideal sheaf `𝓘_Y ⊆ 𝒪_{Y'}`, and let
`g⁻¹(Y) ⊆ X'` be its inverse image (Stacks 083Q).  The converse direction (2) ⟹ (1) of
[Stacks Project, Tag 06BH] needs three facts about this configuration which are read on diagrams
of affine étale scheme charts over `g`; this file proves them, together with the commutative
algebra they feed.

* **Annihilation.**  The defining ideal of `g⁻¹(Y)` annihilates `g^*𝓘_Y`.  On an affine chart
  diagram the sections of `g^*𝓘_Y` are `Γ(U) ⊗_{Γ(V)} J` (`J = 𝓘_Y(V)`), by the chart
  bijectivity of Stacks 083K, and the defining ideal of `g⁻¹(Y)` is generated by the image of `J`;
  an element `g^♯(j)` kills `b ⊗ s` because `j s ∈ J² = 0`.  The affine chart diagrams cover the
  small étale site of `X'`, and `g^*𝓘_Y` is separated, so the annihilation is global.  With the
  essential-image clause of Stacks 08KS this says that the unit `g^*𝓘_Y ⟶ i_*i^*g^*𝓘_Y` is an
  isomorphism.
* **Injectivity on charts.**  If the inverse image along `g` of `𝓘_Y ⟶ 𝒪_{Y'}` is a monomorphism,
  then `Γ(U) ⊗_{Γ(V)} J ⟶ Γ(U) ⊗_{Γ(V)} Γ(V)` is injective on every affine chart diagram: the
  chart comparison of Stacks 083K is natural and bijective at the quasi-coherent `𝓘_Y`.
* **Globalization of flatness.**  A morphism of algebraic spaces is flat (Stacks 03ML part (1))
  as soon as pullback of regular functions is flat along every affine chart diagram: an arbitrary
  chart diagram is covered, Zariski locally on both charts, by restricted affine ones.

The commutative algebra is the converse half of the affine case of Stacks 063Y: from a square-zero
`J`, a flat reduction `Γ(V)/J ⟶ Γ(U)/JΓ(U)` and injectivity of `J ⊗ Γ(U) ⟶ Γ(U)`, the ring map
`Γ(V) ⟶ Γ(U)` is flat (`Ideal.bijective_tensorSMulHomToKer_iff`).

## Main results

* `RingHom.flat_of_injective_lTensor_of_flat_reduction`: the commutative algebra.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.smul_modulePullback_definingIdealSheaf_eq_zero_of_chartDiagram` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.annihilatedByKerIdeal_modulePullback_definingIdealSheaf`: the
  annihilation, on one affine chart diagram and globally.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.injective_lTensor_of_mono_modulePullback_map`: injectivity on charts,
  for a morphism out of any quasi-coherent module.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isFlat_of_flat_chartDiagramRestrict`: flatness of a morphism of
  algebraic spaces from its affine chart diagrams.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.flat_chartDiagramRestrict_of_mono`: the chart flatness of `g` in the
  converse of Stacks 06BH.

## Implementation notes

**This file is separate from `StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.ConormalModuleFlatDeformation`
on purpose.**  The chart bijectivity of Stacks 083K lives in
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.EtaleSourceModuleFMapCompDischarge`, whose closure exposes
the instance candidate recorded in the implementation notes of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Spaces/ConormalModuleBaseChangeFlat.lean`: with it in scope, the
search for `Abelian (Modules.{u, u} …)` aborts with a stuck universe constraint instead of
backtracking.  That module is imported here without `public`, nothing in this file searches for an
abelian structure, and no statement below mentions a privately imported name, so the consumer
keeps its instance searches.

**The commutative algebra takes its hypotheses elementwise.**  The sections of the structure sheaf
over a chart carry two ring structures which agree only up to unfolding: the `RingCat` one, over
which the defining ideals `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.definingIdealAt` are ideals, and the commutative
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartRing_commRing`, over which tensor products and algebras are formed.
Equalities of ideals do not transport between the two, while memberships do by unfolding, so the
square-zero, kernel and range conditions are stated as statements about elements.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 06BH](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/06BH)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 063Y](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/063Y)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 083K](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/083K)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 08KS](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08KS)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03ML](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03ML)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 083Q](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/083Q)
-/

